{
    "comment": [
        "zstd-kmp (com.squareup.zstd:zstd-kmp-jvm) ships no native-image metadata of its own.",
        "Its JNI entry points and the two result fields the C code writes back are only reachable",
        "through native code, so the closed-world analysis would strip them. The native library",
        "itself is loaded at runtime via System.load, so these declarations must be kept as",
        "JNI-accessible for RegisterNatives to bind them. Resources (the jni/<arch>/libzstd-kmp.*",
        "payloads) are embedded via native-image.properties (-H:IncludeResources) in the same dir."
    ],
